 <!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Collage — Privacy Policy</title>

    <meta name="description"
          content="Privacy Policy for Collage — an offline-first quote application.">

    <style>
        :root {
            --background: #f7f7f5;
            --card: #ffffff;
            --text: #1d1d1f;
            --secondary: #6e6e73;
            --border: #e5e5e5;
            --accent: #111111;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        html {
            scroll-behavior: smooth;
        }

        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background: var(--background);
            color: var(--text);
            font-family:
                -apple-system,
                BlinkMacSystemFont,
                "SF Pro Display",
                "SF Pro Text",
                "Helvetica Neue",
                Arial,
                sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        .container {
            width: min(900px, calc(100% - 40px));
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 70px 0 80px;
        }

        .hero {
            margin-bottom: 55px;
        }

        .eyebrow {
            font-size: 13px;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 0.12em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            color: var(--secondary);
            margin-bottom: 18px;
        }

        h1 {
            margin: 0 0 14px;
            font-size: clamp(42px, 8vw, 72px);
            line-height: 1.05;
            letter-spacing: -0.045em;
            font-weight: 750;
        }

        .subtitle {
            font-size: clamp(22px, 4vw, 30px);
            line-height: 1.25;
            letter-spacing: -0.02em;
            color: var(--secondary);
            margin: 0 0 25px;
        }

        .effective-date {
            display: inline-block;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: var(--secondary);
            padding: 8px 14px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 999px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
        }

        .intro {
            font-size: 19px;
            line-height: 1.75;
            color: #444;
            margin: 35px 0 0;
            max-width: 760px;
        }

        .section {
            background: var(--card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 22px;
            padding: 32px 34px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.025);
        }

        .section-header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: baseline;
            gap: 16px;
            margin-bottom: 18px;
        }

        .number {
            font-size: 13px;
            font-weight: 800;
            color: var(--secondary);
            letter-spacing: 0.08em;
            min-width: 24px;
        }

        h2 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 24px;
            line-height: 1.25;
            letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        }

        p {
            margin: 0 0 18px;
            color: #424242;
        }

        p:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        strong {
            color: var(--text);
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .feature-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
            gap: 10px;
            margin: 25px 0;
        }

        .feature {
            padding: 16px 12px;
            text-align: center;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 14px;
            font-size: 13px;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #444;
            background: #fafafa;
        }

        .feature::before {
            content: "✓";
            display: block;
            font-size: 18px;
            font-weight: 800;
            color: var(--accent);
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }

        .highlight {
            padding: 20px 22px;
            margin: 22px 0;
            border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
            background: #f6f6f6;
            border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
            color: #333;
        }

        .contact {
            margin-top: 45px;
            padding: 35px;
            background: var(--text);
            color: white;
            border-radius: 22px;
        }

        .contact h2 {
            color: white;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .contact p {
            color: #d0d0d0;
        }

        .instagram {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 5px;
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 700;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #777;
            padding-bottom: 2px;
        }

        .instagram:hover {
            border-bottom-color: white;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding-top: 40px;
            color: var(--secondary);
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        @media (max-width: 700px) {
            .container {
                width: min(100% - 28px, 900px);
                padding: 45px 0 55px;
            }

            .hero {
                margin-bottom: 35px;
            }

            .section {
                padding: 25px 22px;
                border-radius: 18px;
            }

            .section-header {
                gap: 11px;
            }

            h2 {
                font-size: 21px;
            }

            .intro {
                font-size: 17px;
            }

            .feature-grid {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            }

            .contact {
                padding: 28px 22px;
                border-radius: 18px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<main class="container">

    <!-- HERO -->

    <header class="hero">

        <div class="eyebrow">
            Collage — Privacy Policy
        </div>

        <h1>Your quotes stay on your phone.</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
            Privacy, explained simply.
        </p>

        <div class="effective-date">
            Effective date: September 27, 2026
        </div>

        <p class="intro">
            Collage is built to work offline, on your own device.
            This policy explains, in plain language, exactly what the app
            does and does not do with your information — because the honest
            answer is: almost nothing leaves your phone.
        </p>

    </header>


    <!-- 01 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">01</span>
            <h2>What we collect</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            <strong>Collage does not collect any personal information.</strong>
            There is no account, no sign-in, and no name, email address,
            phone number, or location ever requested or transmitted.
        </p>

        <div class="feature-grid">

            <div class="feature">
                No account required
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                No analytics
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                No advertising
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                No trackers
            </div>

        </div>

        <p>
            Everything you create in the app — favorites, personal notes
            on a quote, words you save, quotes you write yourself — is
            stored in a local database directly on your device, using
            standard iOS storage.
        </p>

        <p>
            We have no access to it and no copy of it exists anywhere else.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- 02 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">02</span>
            <h2>Content syncing</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            Collage downloads its library of quotes, authors, and categories
            from our backend so the app's content can be updated over time.
        </p>

        <div class="highlight">
            This is a one-way content download: your device asks for quotes,
            and quotes are sent back.
        </div>

        <p>
            No personal identifier, account, or usage data is attached to
            that request, and none of your own content — favorites, notes,
            or custom quotes — is ever uploaded to it.
        </p>

        <p>
            Once content has synced, Collage works fully offline.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- 03 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">03</span>
            <h2>Notifications</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            If you turn on the daily quote reminder, it is scheduled
            entirely on your device using iOS's local notification system.
        </p>

        <p>
            No server is involved, no push token is generated, and nothing
            about your reminder schedule is sent anywhere.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- 04 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">04</span>
            <h2>Backup &amp; export</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            If you export your collection to JSON or Excel, that file is
            created and saved through iOS's own share sheet, under your
            control.
        </p>

        <p>
            We never receive a copy of it. Importing quotes works the same
            way, entirely on your device.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- 05 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">05</span>
            <h2>Third parties</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            Collage contains no third-party advertising SDKs, no analytics
            SDKs, and no crash-reporting SDKs.
        </p>

        <p>
            The only network connection the app makes is the one-way
            content sync described above.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- 06 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">06</span>
            <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            Collage does not knowingly collect information from anyone,
            including children, because it does not collect personal
            information from any user.
        </p>

        <p>
            The app is suitable for a general audience.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- 07 -->

    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="number">07</span>
            <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
            If this policy ever changes — for example, if a future feature
            introduces an optional account or a paid subscription — this
            page will be updated and the effective date above will change
            accordingly.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- CONTACT -->

    <section class="contact">

        <h2>Questions about this policy?</h2>

        <p>
            You can contact us through Instagram:
        </p>

        <a
            class="instagram"
            href="https://www.instagram.com/collage_english/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
            @collage_english on Instagram
        </a>

    </section>


    <!-- FOOTER -->

    <footer>

        <p>
            Collage is developed by Barbaros Özdemir.
        </p>

        <p>
            This policy applies to the Collage iOS application.
        </p>

        <p>
            &copy; 2026 Barbaros Özdemir. All rights reserved.
        </p>

    </footer>

</main>

</body>
</html>
